Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0

MICROPOLIS FOR AMIGAOS 3 - EARLY ALPHA
======================================

Micropolis is the open-source version of the original SimCity. This is a port of its
simulation core to the Amiga with a native Intuition front end and RTG graphics
(640x480, 8 bit). Developed and tested with AmigaOS 3.2 only.


REQUIREMENTS
------------
- AmigaOS 3.x, Kickstart 3.2 recommended, 68020 or better (68030/50 MHz is the speed target)
- 2 MB Chip RAM and 2 MB Fast RAM or more
- RTG graphics card with Picasso96 or CyberGraphX (cybergraphics.library 40+) and a screen mode of
  at least 640x480 with 8, 15, 16, 24 or 32 bit (8 bit is used if available).
  In FS-UAE: graphics_card = uaegfx-z3
- LIBS: mathieeedoubbas.library, mathieeedoubtrans.library, gadtools.library, asl.library
  (all are part of a normal Workbench)
- The CPU library for your processor (68030.library, 68040.library, ...) as AmigaOS 3.2 asks for


INSTALLATION
------------
Copy the Micropolis drawer where you like (e.g. Work:) and double-click the Micropolis icon.
Nothing else needs to be installed. The game finds res/ and cities/ next to itself, so it can be
started from anywhere, also from a shell:

    Work:Micropolis/Micropolis                 ; opens cities/haight.cty
    Work:Micropolis/Micropolis my.cty          ; a city file (relative to the current directory)

ToolTypes of the icon (Information): CITY=cities/bruce.cty opens that city at start,
DEBUG writes micropolis.log (also usable as a command line argument).
Startup problems (no RTG, no suitable screen mode, missing data) are reported in a requester.
The Tools drawer has RTGTest (shows a colour gradient in a RTG screen - to check your setup)
and ListModes (lists all screen modes the system knows).


CONTROLS
--------
Tools          click a button on the left (Query, Doze, Road, Rail, Wire, Park, zones,
               Fire, Police, Stadium, power plants, Sea port, Airport)
Build          click or drag on the map; the white frame shows the area
Scroll         W A S D, mouse wheel, mouse at the screen edge; in the overview map click or drag
Menus          right mouse button
Speed          0 pause, 1 slow, 2 medium, 3 fast, P toggles pause
Budget         B, or menu Windows/Budget (Continue or Cancel)
Evaluation     E, or menu Windows/Evaluation (opinion, problems, score)
Graphs         G, or menu Windows/Graphs (6 histories, 10 or 120 years)
Overview map   M on/off, C next overlay (14 overlays in the Map menu)
Quit           Esc, or Project/Quit

The R C I bars at the top right show the demand for residential, commercial and industrial zones.
Warnings and events open a message window (Continue, Return or Space closes it).


STATUS
------
Works: simulation, building tools, animated map, overview map with overlays, budget, evaluation, graphs,
load/save/new random city, menus, disasters, event messages.
Missing: sound, scenario selection, earthquake shake.
An early crash on quitting seems fixed in 0.2 - if you still see it, please report the error number.

micropolis.log is only written with the DEBUG option; attach it to bug reports.
Source code and bug reports: https://github.com/joergsf4/micropolis-amiga


